### III-A Datasets

Datasets pave the way towards the rapid development of 3D data application and exploitation using DL networks. There are two roles of reliable datasets: one for providing a comparison for competing algorithms, another for pushing the fields towards more complex and challenging tasks [[23](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2005.09830#bib.bib23)]. With the increasing application of LiDAR in multiple fields, such as autonomous driving, remote sensing, photogrammetry, there is a rise of large scale datasets with more than millions of points. These datasets accelerate the crucial breakthroughs and unpredicted performance in point cloud segmentation, 3D object detection, and classification. Apart from the mobile LiDAR data, some discriminative datasets [[56](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2005.09830#bib.bib56)] acquired by terrestrial laser scanning (TLS) by static LiDAR are also employed due to they provide high-quality point cloud data.

